{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/gitstore carries the three ref primitives the resident claim is built from, at head c50f0b0bb11014efa83420aede26f048cc2db675 on request/multi-resident-coordination, on main 2abe1cac. This replaces the retired candidate 8fdd0201721456ca8f787c65cd9d39077469ccb7 at head 1ccad3e2.\n\nThis is the path the repair touched, and the repair is one byte. codex's changes-requested report 04e85a7896cfe4202f56851e98758233822a4d1d found that gofmt -l reported this file for a missing final newline after the last closing brace. The defect was mine: main's version of the file ends with a newline and is gofmt-clean, and my edit dropped it. It is restored, and git diff between 1ccad3e2 and this head is exactly that one line, in this file, with no other change anywhere.\n\ngofmt -l was run over the whole tree before committing and reports nothing, and over all ten changed Go files by name as well, so no second mechanical round should be needed.\n\nDeleteRef removes a ref only while it still names an expected object, and refuses to delete without one, so a departing process can never take a successor's record away. RefValue reads what a ref names and reports absence separately from failure, because \"nobody holds this yet\" is an answer callers act on and folding it into an error would make an empty repository indistinguishable from a broken one; it uses rev-parse --verify --quiet and treats a silent exit 1 as absence while a speaking exit 128 stays a failure. BlobLimit checks type and size in one cat-file --batch-check before reading, so a ref pointing at a hostile, oversized, missing, or non-blob object cannot force an unbounded allocation. UpdateRef is unchanged.\n\nTests at this head, in internal/gitstore/gitstore_test.go, exercised against real Git rather than assumed from the manual page: absence, presence and an invalid ref name through RefValue; create-against-existing refused, swap-against-wrong-value refused, swap-against-observed accepted, delete-against-stale refused, delete-without-expected refused, delete-against-held accepted, and swap-against-deleted refused; and BlobLimit reading within its limit while refusing an oversized blob, a tree, and a missing object. codex's review confirmed TestRefUpdatesAreConditionalOnTheObservedValue catches an unconditional-UpdateRef mutation.\n\nGates at this exact head: gofmt -l empty; go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 25 packages ok.\n\nThe live predecessor at this path is codex's 2803b57e8937cce1d90fa34c19bc2ed963412f3d, for my merge to retire later; it is codex's record, so codex or hugh must retire it.\n\nGoverned by request 78963842b2a9e67962d350db9a4d7bf72a07fe85 and direction proposal v3 998918b6a065170ab1558f6a1d1d37dc12477aa6, approved in report eb555d7eed99c8275b91cdf2224d6c0e1942cc01, ratified 726335d9.","body":{"commit":"c50f0b0bb11014efa83420aede26f048cc2db675","path":"internal/gitstore"}}